            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0227" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>

                <head>71. Memorandum From Acting Secretary of State Christopher to President Carter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d71-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-05-12">May 12, 1977</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to India.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Nuclear Supply to India.</hi> We will inform the Indian
                    Ambassador tomorrow that we have decided to recommend an interim supply of
                    low-enriched uranium for India on condition that they agree to early
                    negotiations with us on outstanding nuclear issues. Our Charge in New Delhi will
                    make a parallel approach there and we will be advising concerned members of
                    Congress of the decision. When we receive official confirmation of India’s
                    willingness to negotiate, we will advise the Nuclear Regulatory Commission of
                    Executive Branch support for the shipment. Making an interim shipment such as we
                    envisage will provide time to see whether a satisfactory understanding on
                    nuclear matters can be worked out with Desai and his new government.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d71-f2"/></p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to India.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d71-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d71-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 18, Evening Reports (State): 5/77. Secret. In the upper right-hand
                    corner of the memorandum, Carter wrote:
                    “To Warren, J.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d71-f2" n="2" xml:id="d71-f2-content">
                <p>In the left-hand margin next to this paragraph, Carter wrote: “Do not ship India any fuel unless they agree to
                    the strictest international safeguards—Similar to what Canada demands.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
